## 1. Circuit V=392 re-partition (M67 step 5)

Graph (Stim `rotated_memory_z` d=3 r=3, all four noise families at p=0.02, `dem_to_payload` `^`-split):

| | phenom (M70) | circuit (M76) |
|---|---|---|
| detectors D | 24 | 24 |
| degree-1 pieces (unique virtual boundaries) | 48 | **368** |
| V | 72 | 392 |
| max boundaries on one detector | 3 | **35** |
| detector components | 2 | 2 |

**Why M70 schemes fail on circuit:** both `det_comp_paired` and `one_det` put every boundary in its detector's part, so the worst part needs ≥ 1 + 35 = 36 distinct physical PEs > N_PHYS=16 (`need more than 16 colors`). Merging parallel boundary pieces would change edge weights/goldens and is close to the rejected shared-boundary shortcut (Progress mistakes) — **not done**.

**Feasible scheme (new, fallback only):** `det_comp_paired_overflow` — paired parts capped at N_PHYS nodes; overflow boundaries go to extra parts. An overflow edge (det, b) is cross-cut, so b colocates with det's class (Helios rule), hence each extra part holds ≤1 overflow boundary per detector component. Evaluated only when the M70 schemes fail, so phenom outputs stay byte-identical (`cmp` vs cited `helios_n_coloring_m70*.csv`).

| Result | Value |
|---|---|
| n_parts | **165** (lower bound ⌈392/16⌉ = 25) |
| phys colors | 16 |
| max part size | 16 |
| induced / cross edges | 182 / 374 |
| max virtual nodes on one PE | 165 |
| M71 oracle (grow ≡ flat) | **16/16** (`results/helios_n_grow_cosim_circuit_m76.csv`) |
| M72 oracle (grow→peel ≡ decode_cosim) | **16/16** (`results/helios_n_decode_cosim_circuit_m76.csv`) |

Map: `results/helios_n_coloring_circuit_m76*.csv` via `scripts/helios_n_coloring_m70.py --noise circuit --p 0.02 --prefix helios_n_coloring_circuit_m76`.

**Interpretation:** legal under transitive Helios colocation, but the transitive closure piles each detector component plus its overflow boundaries onto one PE (165 contexts) — the M74 schedule would be 2·165+2 = 332 clk per growth iteration. Not an efficient mapping; it is the measured cost of (unique boundaries × transitive colocation). Better options need a decision: (a) non-transitive cross-cut wiring (Heer-style ports — reject without a paper per M67), (b) boundary-piece merging with re-validated goldens, (c) larger N_PHYS.

